{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>The sons of Rachel, wife of Jacob.</b> She was the primary object of his intention. From her were born <b>Joseph and Benjamin</b>, who were the most excellent among the tribes, as the Sages said, of blessed memory (Sotah 36b). Joseph was worthy that twelve tribes should come forth from him just as from Jacob — and as the Sages said, of blessed memory (Shabbat 55b), concerning Benjamin, that he died by the kiss of the serpent. And so Scripture testifies, saying: לְפָנִים אֶפְרַיִם וּבִנְיָמִן וּמְנַשֶּׁה עוֹרְרָה אֶת גְּבוּרָתֶךָ (Psalms 80:3)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {0 "The word בְּעֶטְיוֹ appears to be a variant spelling of בִּנְשׁוּקָה or similar; the idiom 'kiss of the serpent' renders it hyper-literally per the instruction for obscure readings. Sforno's citation of Psalms 80:3 follows the verse numbering in the Hebrew text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:53.724934776Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}